A||||5||Klown||Wheel/Tire diameter and acceleration.||||5||
Z||000000||Klown||05-13-2000||05:29 PM||||I was wondering if anyone could tell me how the overall wheel/tire diameter affects acceleration and top speed.  I am currently running 225/60-15's which have a diameter of roughly 25.5 inches.  I was thinking of switching over to 225/50-15's which have a diameter of almost 24 inches.  Would this drop of 1.5 inches in diameter affect my gearing enough to give me a little better acceleration or would the difference be negligible.  Thanks for the help.||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||05-13-2000||05:42 PM||||I went from 60/16's to 50/16's on my old '85 IROC and I DID notice a slight different in acceleration.  Of course, that may also be attributed to the fact that the 50's were Z rated, and the 60's were crap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||05-13-2000||05:44 PM||||keep in mind, the 50's will make the wheel wells look larger which some people don't like.  I thought it looked pretty nice.  You may want to try 55's.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Klown||05-13-2000||06:40 PM||||I've been looking for a 225/55-15 for a while now but I haven't been able to find one at the local tire shops.  Would you happen to know a manufacturer that makes them?||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||05-13-2000||07:46 PM||||HOOSIER and MICHELIN<P>The hoosiers are slicks though...hehe.  check out Tirerack.com||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||05-13-2000||10:49 PM|||| <A HREF="http://powerdog.com/tiresize.cgi" TARGET=_blank>http://powerdog.com/tiresize.cgi</A> <P>The above link will take you to a site that you can enter up to 10 tire sizes (including your stock size) and it will give you all the dimensions of the tire and give you a speedo error factor.||||reg||1
